kb/sources/russell-wefald-principles-of-metareasoning.ingest.md:152:   simplification comes from using both together: relaxing either one alone
kb/sources/pathway-beyond-transformers-sudoku-bench.ingest.md:40:- [codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) -- **exemplifies**: BDH's "latent reasoning space" is an architectural relaxing move replacing codified chain-of-thought.
kb/sources/hacker-news-llm-voice.ingest.md:36:For the supplied occasion, the settled connection is a public restatement of [LLM generation can hide a relaxed goal where human writing exposes a stall](../theory/llm-generation-relaxes-goals-where-human-writing-stalls.md). Comment [50301386](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50301386) offers a broader gap-filling model; [50301441](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50301441) explicitly refers back to that note and credits Borretti. This is feedback from the KB into discussion, not independent corroboration. The note specifies what the comment leaves open: fluent output can satisfy a weaker goal while concealing an unmet constraint, but failure to find a satisfying artifact does not prove the original goal impossible. Helpful elaboration and concealed failure must therefore be distinguished by checking the requirements, not merely by labeling all completion hallucination.
kb/sources/hacker-news-llm-voice.ingest.md:61:The maintainer's own comments cannot independently support the KB theory they repeat. As the [hidden-goal-relaxation note](../theory/llm-generation-relaxes-goals-where-human-writing-stalls.md) itself cautions, its mechanism is conjectural and scope-bound. The thread adds reactions and candidate checks, not evidence of the mechanism's prevalence. Claims about useful model-facing content likewise lack an observed downstream consumption path.
kb/sources/hacker-news-llm-voice.ingest.md:65:File this ingest as a source-only reference for comments 50301386–50301441 and their surrounding discussion, without promoting those comments as independent evidence for the hidden-goal-relaxation note.
kb/sources/darwin-godel-machine-open-ended-evolution-self-improving-agents.ingest.md:22:The Darwin Gödel Machine evolves coding-agent implementations around frozen foundation models. Each iteration samples a parent from a growing archive with probability rising in benchmark score and falling in its count of functioning children, feeds that parent's evaluation logs to a separate o1 diagnostic call that names one general improvement, has the selected agent implement the change in its own Python repository, evaluates the child on a staged benchmark subset, and admits it to the archive if it still compiles and can edit code. Over 80 iterations the reported best agent rises from 20.0% to 50.0% on the SWE-bench Verified subsets used and from 14.2% to 30.7% on full Polyglot, discovering finer-grained file viewing and string-replacement editing, context auto-summarization, retries and patch validation, and multi-candidate generation with an FM ranker. Ablations that fix the modifier to the base agent (39.0% / 28.0%), keep only the latest agent (23.0% / 14.0%), or always branch from the current best (39.7% / 30.0%) all underperform. The paper positions itself explicitly as relaxing Schmidhuber's proof requirement in favour of empirical evidence, and an appendix reports an objective-hacking episode in which an agent deleted the tool-use markers its evaluator depended on.
kb/sources/darwin-godel-machine-open-ended-evolution-self-improving-agents.ingest.md:56:> A Gödel Machine is a theoretical idea of an AI that searches for ways that provably improve itself (Schmidhuber, 2007). In this paper, we propose Darwin Gödel Machine (DGM), an attempt to realize the long-held dream of creating a Gödel Machine. The DGM relaxes the Gödel Machine’s impractical requirement of theoretically proving that a change will improve the system, instead requiring empirical evidence from experiments to demonstrate that a proposed new version enhances performance.
kb/sources/darwin-godel-machine-open-ended-evolution-self-improving-agents.ingest.md:64:This source is the anchor case the KB's self-improvement-loop cluster was missing: the most-cited system in the 2026 neighbourhood, already named in [the omitted/frozen mapping note](../theory/an-omitted-loop-function-and-a-frozen-one-need-different-repairs.md) without having been read. It is the empirical counterpart to [Gödel machines are a proof-governed case of reflective self-modification](../theory/goedel-machines-are-a-proof-governed-case-of-self-modification.md), and the paper settles the lineage question in the KB's favour and in its own words: DGM "relaxes the Gödel Machine's impractical requirement of theoretically proving that a change will improve the system," on the stated ground that such proofs are impossible without restrictive assumptions. The departure is the authors' declared design choice, not an outside reading.
kb/sources/darwin-godel-machine-open-ended-evolution-self-improving-agents.ingest.md:66:The mechanism, though, is looser than "benchmark gate" implies, and that is where this source most sharpens existing claims. Algorithm 1 admits every child that compiles and retains codebase-editing functionality; benchmark score never decides admission, only the sampling weight over future parents. Read against [the search, evaluation, and operative retention decomposition](../theory/a-proposal-selection-loop-requires-search-evaluation-and-retention.md), the reject-capable operation in DGM is a viability filter and the score is a search signal. The Gödel machine's tight coupling of evaluation to authority — the proof checker both licenses and installs the rewrite — is therefore not weakened in DGM but dissolved: quality evidence and operative retention became separate subsystems. Nothing is ever retired from the archive either, which makes DGM a fifth case for the retirement gap the mapping note leaves open ([retire, redact, supersede, relax](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/retire-redact-supersede-relax.md)) and the one case where the omission is deliberate.
kb/sources/past-bench-personal-agents-pdf.ingest.md:37:The paper also gives bounded evidence for [Activate Behavior-Changing Memory Before The Mistake](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/activate-behavior-changing-memory.md) and [Retire, Redact, Supersede, And Relax Memory](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/retire-redact-supersede-relax.md). In the tested Hermes substrate, pre-answer retrieval gating improves Information Gathering, while rendering valid bindings and persisting corrections address stale-state failures. These are tests of runtime changes around existing interfaces. They do not establish that typed bindings or the memory/skill/history split are preferable to alternative representations, and the lifecycle evidence concerns correction and expiry rather than redaction or policy relaxation.
kb/sources/hacker-news-im-becoming-ai-blind.ingest.md:29:The thread serves as a qualitative field corpus for [reverse compression](../theory/reverse-compression-is-when-llm-output-expands-without-adding.md), especially the claim that a longer artifact can leave the reader to recover a much smaller payload. Reports of polished pseudo-language and plans whose missing high-level logic must be reconstructed also bear on [hidden constraint relaxation](../theory/llm-generation-relaxes-goals-where-human-writing-stalls.md). Workplace triage accounts support [cheap generation breaking text volume as an effort signal](../theory/cheap-generation-breaks-text-volume-as-an-effort-signal.md), while the false-positive and high-quality-output counterexamples reinforce that this signal is not an AI detector. Relative to the [original essay ingest](./im-becoming-ai-blind.ingest.md), the discussion's main role is to broaden the candidate failure inventory and supply boundaries; its recurring distinction between polished topical coverage and an actual contribution also exemplifies why [warranted reader update](../theory/warranted-reader-update-is-the-objective-of-substantive-writing.md) is a better objective than stylistic fluency.
kb/sources/eric-evans-ai-components-deterministic-system.ingest.md:40:- **[codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md)** — exemplifies: Evans' incremental updates pattern (check against existing categories, add genuinely new ones) is the relax/re-codify cycle operating on a taxonomy.
kb/sources/eric-evans-ai-components-deterministic-system.ingest.md:48:3. **The incremental update pattern** — prompting the LLM to check new items against an existing category set and only add genuinely new ones. This is a concrete implementation of the relax/re-codify cycle: the categories are mostly frozen but have a controlled expansion path. [experiment] — could inform how we handle schema evolution in the KB's own type system.
kb/sources/towards-a-science-of-ai-agent-reliability.ingest.md:37:3. **[relaxing-signals](../theory/operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md)** -- grounds: R_prompt operationalises brittleness-under-paraphrase as a quantitative metric at scale. The counterintuitive finding (models handle real faults but break under rephrasings) is the relaxing signal pattern confirmed across 14 models.
kb/sources/towards-a-science-of-ai-agent-reliability.ingest.md:53:2. **Prompt robustness as the weakest link.** Models handle genuine infrastructure faults (API timeouts, malformed responses) but break under semantically equivalent instruction rephrasings. This is counterintuitive and actionable: invest in prompt robustness testing before worrying about fault tolerance. Already captured in relaxing-signals note. [just-a-reference]
kb/sources/symbols-neural-networks-mathematical-intelligence.ingest.md:45:The source's main KB role is a **formal-domain case for relaxing** and a **cognitive-science counterpart to the KB's symbolic/parametric split**. It adds no new mechanism to either.
kb/sources/symbols-neural-networks-mathematical-intelligence.ingest.md:47:The IMO sequence is the first formal-reasoning instance in the KB's bitter-lesson cluster. It illustrates the absorption half of [scaling absorbs scaffolding at fixed task difficulty, not at the deployment frontier](../theory/scaling-absorbs-scaffolding-at-fixed-difficulty-not-at-the-frontier.md) (is-evidence-for). Olympiad problems stay fixed in difficulty while the Lean scaffold disappears across model generations. The note's "Observed at both ends" section currently has only practitioner cases. The case also illustrates relaxing in [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) (is-evidence-for), whose examples come from vision and hardware. In both uses the comparison changes the model, training, compute, and reasoning medium together. It therefore illustrates absorption and does not isolate the removal of the formal constraint as the cause. The essay is silent on the frontier-recurrence half of the scaling note: it says solvers "may" have been used for the conjecture results and sets that aside.
kb/sources/symbols-neural-networks-mathematical-intelligence.ingest.md:59:**Mapping onto Commonplace concepts.** Internalization is movement of competence from the symbolic form into the distributed-parametric form. This fits the coevolution note's framing and supports it only illustratively: the essay asserts the transfer and does not show it for the IMO systems. Across system generations, removing the Lean constraint is relaxing, but the retraining that relaxed it was done by the lab through gradient-based training. The system that did the relaxing is therefore not the one solving problems. The external solver used "for verification" is the closest match to content-directed criticism of a stated artifact. The essay places it outside intelligence. The KB would place it inside the criticism loop of a theory builder. This is a difference in what each account is about, not a factual conflict.
kb/sources/symbols-neural-networks-mathematical-intelligence.ingest.md:77:2. **A formal-domain relaxing instance** -- the relaxing examples in the codification-and-relaxing note come from vision and hardware. A case in theorem proving, where codification looks safest, extends the note's range. The relaxed component was the reasoning medium, and the symbolic checker stays available as an optional external tool, which matches the note's hybrid conclusion. [quick-win]
kb/sources/symbols-neural-networks-mathematical-intelligence.ingest.md:78:3. **A distinction between verification inside and outside the generation loop** -- the essay separates solving (in prose) from optional external checking. Together with the scaling and relaxing notes, this suggests a conjecture: formal verification inside the reasoning loop is absorbable at fixed difficulty, while verification of a finished result persists. One essay's reading of announcements is too thin to write that as a note now. [experiment]
kb/sources/dreamcoder-wake-sleep-bayesian-program-learning.ingest.md:59:The gate is also a proxy the paper does not separate from what it stands in for. Description length is measured over already-solved training programs; nothing in the criterion sees held-out generalization. Held-out performance is reported and is good, but the causal link from "shortens the training corpus" to "transfers" is asserted by correlation (the r=0.79 depth-performance figure) rather than isolated by an ablation that varies the gate while holding search fixed. The baselines compare against weaker search (enumeration, exploration-compression, RobustFill on the initial library) and against memorization, but not against a strong human-authored DSL for the same domain -- the comparison that would tell us whether learned libraries beat expert-designed ones, which is the question [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) actually cares about.
kb/sources/dulleck-kerschbamer-doctors-mechanics-computer-specialists.ingest.md:22:A credence good is one whose consumer cannot judge, even after the fact, whether the quality he received was the quality he needed — a car repair, a medical treatment, a computer spec. Only the expert seller knows, and can exploit that asymmetry by overtreating, undertreating, or overcharging. The literature had produced a confusing spread of contradictory results; this paper collapses them into one simple binary model. Its central result: market institutions eliminate expert fraud at zero cost if and only if three conditions hold — (i) large economies of scope between diagnosis and treatment, (ii) either the treatment type is *verifiable* or a *liability* rule protects the consumer (or both), and (iii) homogeneous consumers. Relaxing any single condition reproduces essentially every known inefficiency in the literature: violate (ii) with neither verifiability nor liability and the market breaks down entirely, a hidden-action Akerlof lemons case. The paper is a canonical microeconomic formalization of the exact variable this KB treats as structural: whether the consumer of an output can verify its quality — and it adds that a liability rule can substitute for verifiability to reach the same efficient outcome.
kb/sources/sean-goedecke-what-requirements-dont-you-have.ingest.md:45:5. **Design-elegance examples** -- The Unicorn, S3, StatsD, SQLite and edge-cache cases illustrate requirement relaxation in general system design. That is outside this KB's scope except as background. [just-a-reference]
kb/sources/sean-goedecke-what-requirements-dont-you-have.ingest.md:49:The agent claims rest on one engineer's review experience. "About half the time", "invariably" and "in every single system I've worked on" are unquantified, unsampled and self-reported; no diff, task or model is named. The causal story, that RLVR training produces grader-obsessed over-satisfaction, is a plausible framing but is not tested. A simpler account fits the same observations: an underspecified prompt admits many designs, and any interpreter without business context will choose some extra guards. Distinguishing a training-induced bias from ordinary underspecification would need comparison against human engineers or differently trained models given the same tasks. The source does not show that the added checks were harmful in the reviewed cases rather than merely unnecessary, and the "petrify" claim is a forecast with no longitudinal evidence. Survivorship also applies: Goedecke reports the requirements he caught, not those he missed or those that turned out to be needed. The essay's argument that elegance comes from dropped requirements is persuasive in its chosen examples, but selected successes do not show how often relaxing a requirement goes wrong.
kb/sources/05-attention-is-all-you-need.ingest.md:22:The chapter explains the Transformer by reconstructing the problems it relaxed: a fixed thought vector compressing an entire sequence, recurrence creating long information and gradient paths, arbitrary ordering burdening set tasks, and sequential execution limiting parallel scale. Bahdanau attention lets a decoder query encoder states; pointer networks turn attention into an output mechanism; Neural Turing Machines add differentiable addressing; order experiments expose serialization as a hidden design choice; and self-attention removes recurrence while retaining positional, residual, normalization, masking, and feed-forward structure. The historical reversal trick provides a particularly clear example of temporary scaffolding whose benefit vanished as architecture changed.
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:2:description: "Awareness Requirements make requirement-state monitoring explicit, but leave goal authority, proxy validity and knowledge revision outside the demonstrated loop."
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:13:domains: [awareness-requirements, requirements-monitoring, goal-oriented-requirements-engineering, self-adaptive-systems]
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:21:A SEAMS 2011 research paper proposing a requirements category, formalization patterns and a prototype monitoring implementation, evaluated through constructed scenarios and a small performance experiment. Authors Vítor E. Silva Souza, Alexei Lapouchnian, William N. Robinson and John Mylopoulos were affiliated with Trento, Toronto and Georgia State; Robinson's EEAT requirements-monitoring framework supplies the implementation baseline.
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:25:Awareness Requirements (AwReqs) specify constraints on the runtime states of other requirements or domain assumptions: never fail, succeed at a specified rate over a time window, avoid declining success rates, or complete within a time bound. They can also refer to other AwReqs in successive strata. The paper connects stakeholder goals and qualitative softgoals to measurable quality constraints, then to requirements about their observed satisfaction. Requirements become monitor-side UML classes and runtime instances, with temporal constraints expressed in OCL with Temporal Message logic and compiled by EEAT into event-processing rules. Constructed scenarios reportedly yield the expected satisfaction verdicts within this instrumented class-and-event representation; they do not compare alternative goal decompositions or demonstrate successful end-to-end adaptation. Compensation, diagnosis and systematic construction of a complete monitor-analyze-plan-execute loop remain future work.
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:29:The important contribution appears to be making the requirements problem behind feedback infrastructure explicit: critical requirements may fail, so their acceptable runtime behavior itself needs specification. Named patterns and executable monitoring make that proposal inspectable and testable rather than merely redescribing adaptivity. The scenario tests establish limited feasibility, not improved resilience, and the comparisons with RELAX, FLAGS and probabilistic goal satisfaction are conceptual rather than controlled evaluations. The paper plausibly contributes a useful modeling interface, but its stronger practical significance depends on whether the missing diagnosis and compensation stages improve outcomes without merely weakening targets. The available comparisons do not establish broad originality or superiority.
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:43:The proposed adaptation mechanism is a feedback loop driven by violations of explicit requirements about other requirements. Only its monitoring stage is implemented here. Meta-AwReq examples suggest escalation, changing success-rate targets, or temporarily disabling a requirement to avoid repeated notifications. These are illustrations of possible reconciliation policies, not evaluated learning algorithms. The paper's “awareness” means reference to requirement states, not consciousness; its goal decomposition is not itself Commonplace's technical concept of program refinement.
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:47:The implementation retains runtime evaluation objects and temporal event histories for monitoring. The paper does not establish reuse of revisions or critical records across runs or problems. Nor does it report improved capacity for future action. Relative to [learning inside a fixed decomposition](../theory/learning-inside-a-fixed-decomposition-inherits-its-mistakes.md), the tests hold requirement classes, event mappings and satisfaction semantics fixed. Proposed target relaxation changes a parameter within that representation; it does not establish that the system can revise the representation or its governing purpose. The source supports separating observable violation from diagnosis and revision, rather than treating monitoring as sufficient for learning.
kb/sources/awareness-requirements-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:64:Several textual details need checking before implementation: section 5.1's prose for AR8 reverses the temporal ordering stated in Table 1 and section 4, and Table 2 uses strict inequalities where some pattern descriptions suggest inclusive bounds. The plain-text capture does not preserve full graphical notation, so these are reasons to consult the published figures and specifications rather than copy extracted idioms as authoritative code. Full adaptation and compensation remain future work; threshold relaxation is not evidence that the revised target better serves the original purpose.
kb/sources/prime-agent-a-self-improving-rlm-harness.ingest.md:26:Prime Agent combines a persistent IPython environment, daemon-owned recursive sessions, family-scoped messaging, versioned prompt/memory/skill/subagent state, long-horizon controls, and descendant-aware resource accounting into one agent harness. The paper argues that this expressive substrate lets a fixed model construct its own information-management and orchestration strategies, then reports results across ARC-AGI-3, long-context tasks, coding benchmarks, nanoGPT, Factorio, and MazeBench. For this KB, its strongest contribution is not the headline performance: it is a concrete runtime decomposition plus a failure case in which online refinement preserved a Factorio specification exploit as a reusable skill. That combination makes the source useful for reasoning about persistence boundaries, behavior-changing-write authority, and the limits of bundle-level harness evaluations.
kb/sources/tarski-semantic-conception-of-truth.ingest.md:85:   *It cannot draw:* (a) a theorem about natural language "as a whole". The results apply only to exactly specified languages, and Tarski says the consistency question is not exactly meaningful for everyday language. (b) An "in principle" impossibility that does not depend on assumptions. The result binds only together with classical logic and full disquotation, and the post-1944 literature relaxes exactly those (background knowledge, not from the source). (c) Anything about *executable* semantics. Tarski's barrier concerns defining truth within the same language. An operational semantics fixes execution, not truth. Self-interpreting programming languages and universal machines run programs of a language rich enough to talk about computation. Halting-style results forbid *deciding* properties, not *executing* (our inference). (d) A contrast between natural and programming languages. Undefinability and the lack of a truth criterion hit formalized arithmetic just as much, so they cannot be what separates natural language from programming languages. The defensible core is narrower: a natural language used as its own complete metalanguage cannot also be exactly specified, classical and fully disquotational. In addition, a specified fragment (Tarski's approximation) is what any codification fixes.
kb/sources/tarski-semantic-conception-of-truth.ingest.md:93:The paper gives no proofs. Every formal claim, including necessity and sufficiency of essential richness and the reconstruction of the liar without the empirical premise (note 11, which Tarski admits is unclear in "in what sense"), rests on the 1933/1935 work. "Essential richness" is defined precisely only for type-theoretic languages, so its general scope is asserted, not shown. Statements about natural language are informal and hedged, and none is a theorem. Anyone citing the paper for a natural-language impossibility result cites the hedges, not the theorems. The 1944 framing is dated in a way that affects reuse. Assumption (II) is held fixed by decision. Kripke-style partial truth predicates and paraconsistent semantics later showed that relaxing (II) or full disquotation yields languages that contain their own truth predicate in a restricted sense. Our knowledge of those developments is background, not in this source. The "universality of colloquial language" argument is in the 1933 monograph and not here, so this ingest cannot ground it. The transcription has visible errors, for example "on tile left side", the satisfaction example rendered as "2 is white", a bibliography date of "1911" for *Fundamenta* XVII, and a table-of-contents heading for section 8 ending in "?" that the body heading lacks. Liar-sentence page references ("p. 347, l. 31") point to the original journal pagination. For exact wording at a contested point, check against the printed paper.
kb/sources/jdegoes-recursive-agent-architecture-2081854216264392934.ingest.md:40:4. **Compiled guardrails are a strong witness for the codification side of the verifiability gradient.** Middleware can turn a rule with a formal-enough meaning into an enforced property rather than a context-dependent request. The source is most useful here as a counterpoint: it treats the remaining natural-language text as decoration, while Commonplace preserves judgment-bearing natural language and a reverse relaxing path. [experiment]
kb/sources/the-mismanaged-geniuses-hypothesis-2042588627260018751.ingest.md:38:A prior `/connect` pass found a tight Scheduling & Orchestration cluster. The strongest connections are to [RLM has the model write ephemeral orchestrators over sub-agents](../theory/rlm-has-the-model-write-ephemeral-orchestrators-over-sub-agents.md), which MGH extends from RLM mechanism to learned decomposition policy; [Bounded-context orchestration model](../theory/bounded-context-orchestration-model.md), which MGH restates as a model-management bottleneck where OOD tasks are solved by composing in-distribution calls; [Decomposition heuristics for bounded-context scheduling](../theory/decomposition-heuristics-for-bounded-context-scheduling.md), which MGH extends by making the decomposition space itself the exponential design variable; and [Agent orchestration occupies a multi-dimensional design space](../theory/agent-orchestration-occupies-a-multi-dimensional-design-space.md), which MGH suggests should add an axis for decomposition-policy acquisition and training. It also connects to [Codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) because the source argues for relaxing hand-engineered scaffold choice into learned behavior while retaining a codified scaffold/decomposition language.
kb/sources/the-mismanaged-geniuses-hypothesis-2042588627260018751.ingest.md:44:2. **Training over a scaffold as codify/relax hybrid** — MGH does not say "remove scaffolds." It says define the decomposition space, then train the model to perform correct decompositions inside it. That is a clean hybrid: codify the action/decomposition language, relax the policy that uses it. [experiment] High reach: this sharpens the bitter-lesson boundary for agent harnesses.
kb/sources/the-mismanaged-geniuses-hypothesis-2042588627260018751.ingest.md:66:Update [agent-orchestration-occupies-a-multi-dimensional-design-space.md](../theory/agent-orchestration-occupies-a-multi-dimensional-design-space.md): add a dimension for **decomposition-policy acquisition** — human-engineered scaffold, model-authored ephemeral program, artifact-mined/versioned policy, or trained policy over a scaffold. Cite this source as the argument for the trained-policy end of the axis, and link it to [RLM has the model write ephemeral orchestrators over sub-agents](../theory/rlm-has-the-model-write-ephemeral-orchestrators-over-sub-agents.md) and [Codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md).
kb/sources/memorylace-lifecycle-aware-consolidation-evidence-retrieval.ingest.md:31:The paper supplies a bounded empirical case for [Retire, Redact, Supersede, And Relax Memory](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/retire-redact-supersede-relax.md): superseded entries leave ordinary active retrieval, but remain recoverable through their successors. Temporal metadata helps distinguish an ordered update from a same-scope conflict. The tested mechanism addresses supersession and temporal validity, not the note's redaction, retirement, or policy-relaxation requirements.
kb/sources/requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md:2:description: "A 2010 design proposal reifies requirements as runtime objects and synchronizes them with architecture, providing a structural precedent for causal self-representation without evidence of conjectural learning."
kb/sources/requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md:7:capture_url: https://publications.aston.ac.uk/id/eprint/19494/1/Requirements_as_runtime_entities.pdf
kb/sources/requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md:16:# Ingest: Requirements Reflection: Requirements as Runtime Entities
kb/sources/requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md:24:The paper argues that requirements monitoring leaves a running system with low-level derived artifacts but not the high-level goals, assumptions, alternatives, and relationships that motivated them. It proposes reifying those requirements as first-class runtime entities in a goal-oriented meta-model, exposing operations for inspecting and changing them, and semantically synchronizing that requirements stratum with a reflective architecture stratum so changes on either side can affect or be checked against the other. It also proposes runtime reasoning about uncertainty and interactive multi-objective trade-offs. Read it as a concrete structural agenda for putting a software system's purposes on a causal path to adaptation, not as evidence that the architecture works or that the system learns its own requirements model.
kb/sources/requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md:37:2. **The represented vocabulary determines the available questions and interventions** -- A KAOS-like meta-model would let a system navigate goal relations, identify responsible agents, inspect assumptions, and invoke operations such as adding, deleting, replacing, or assigning requirements and goals. This gives a concrete requirements-specific instance of runtime representation creating a control surface. [quick-win]
kb/sources/requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md:39:4. **Most of the effective update space remains designer-supplied** -- The paper leaves the goal language and meta-model, exposed primitives, requirements-to-architecture mapping, monitoring boundary, uncertainty formalism, decision procedure, and human interaction policy to designers. Runtime reprioritization or replacement therefore occurs inside a fixed decomposition rather than revising the machinery that defines valid representations and adaptations. [deep-dive]
kb/sources/claude-workstream-kit-fable-agent-scaffolding.ingest.md:2:description: "claude-workstream-kit announcement arguing that stronger models relax model-management scaffolding but make project-scoped, git-versioned active work state more important"
kb/sources/claude-workstream-kit-fable-agent-scaffolding.ingest.md:56:4. **Strong models relax proxy scaffolding but not authority constraints** -- The source reports that Fable followed principle-level instructions well enough to remove multi-phase checklists, compliance scripts, and sync layers, while preserving human-authority constraints such as no self-certifying closure and checkbox completion with cited evidence. This is a precise boundary case for the KB's scaffold-relaxation theory. [quick-win]
kb/sources/induction-bias-sequence-models-ebrahimi-2026.ingest.md:61:- [codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) -- **grounds**: Step-by-step decomposition is a permanent architectural advantage for state tracking, not a temporary one that scale dissolves. The kappa results show that the general method (transformer) not only fails to scale past the constraint -- it actively degrades (destructive interference) when exposed to more diverse data.
kb/sources/voooooogel-multi-agent-future.ingest.md:33:**Grounding the KB's learning-theory cluster.** The source's entire argument is an applied [bitter-lesson-boundary](../theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md) analysis: filesystem and multi-agent parallelism survive because they're structural (spec IS the problem), while fixed role hierarchies are vision features (theories about how to organize agents). It directly exemplifies the [codification-and-relaxing](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) framework — current orchestration patterns are codifications that will relax when scale makes model-discovered decompositions viable. Specific relaxing signals from the [relaxing-signals](../theory/operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md) catalogue are identifiable in the source's examples.
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:2:description: "A 2010 research agenda extends requirements reflection into runtime model evolution, uncertainty, trade-offs, and explanation, supplying structural lineage rather than outcome evidence."
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:20:This is a scientific research-agenda paper from the 2010 IEEE Requirements Engineering Conference. It synthesizes prior requirements-engineering and self-adaptive-systems work into a proposed architecture and five research challenges; it does not report an implementation or an evaluation of requirements reflection. Author: five Lancaster University and University College London researchers working across requirements engineering, goal modeling, reflective middleware, and self-adaptive systems, with the paper's argument grounded in those literatures and the authors' related RELAX work.
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:24:The paper argues that a self-adaptive system operating in a volatile, imperfectly understood environment should keep its requirements model as a runtime entity rather than as passive design-time documentation. Its proposed requirements stratum exposes goals, assumptions, alternatives, conflicts, responsibilities, and satisfaction relations for inspection and manipulation, while semantic synchronization with a reflective architecture stratum is meant to carry requirements changes into system reconfiguration and check architectural changes against requirements. The resulting agenda covers runtime representation, model evolution and synchronization, uncertainty, multi-objective choice, and self-explanation. Read it as a detailed conceptual map of requirements-aware adaptation and its unresolved dependencies, not as evidence that the proposed causal loop works.
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:32:Its primary role is a companion expansion of [Requirements Reflection: Requirements as Runtime Entities](./requirements-reflection-runtime-entities.ingest.md), not an independent confirmation: it substantially repeats the runtime-object and two-stratum proposal while adding a five-part agenda and fuller treatments of uncertainty, interactive trade-offs, and explanation. For [Theory building has distinct epistemic, structural, and implementation precedents](../theory/theory-building-has-distinct-precedents.md), it is a requirements-specific structural basis and limitation: a representation of the running system's own goals and assumptions is placed on a proposed causal path to architectural change, but no empirical theory-refinement or independently evaluated read-back loop is supplied. Its designer-set modeling language, monitors, transformation operators, and cross-stratum mappings also make it a concrete comparison for [Learning inside a fixed decomposition inherits its mistakes](../theory/learning-inside-a-fixed-decomposition-inherits-its-mistakes.md).
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:38:3. **The effective update space includes goal operations but excludes most adaptation machinery** -- The proposed primitives can add, delete, or replace requirements and goals, reassign agents, choose alternatives, relax satisfaction, and trigger component reconfiguration. The goal language and meta-model, sensed variables, monitoring boundary, valid component set, transformation library, requirements-to-architecture semantics, uncertainty formalism, decision procedure, and explanation policy remain designer-supplied; the paper gives no mechanism for learning or replacing them from outcomes. [deep-dive]
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:40:5. **The evidence establishes a motivated proposal, not adaptive effectiveness** -- The paper combines prior literature, illustrative systems and scenarios, a proposed meta-object structure, and RELAX's formal semantics. It reports no requirements-reflection implementation, benchmark, ablation, or outcome data; it explicitly notes that RELAX had no runtime-monitoring implementation, and the cited explanation experiment evaluates another context-aware-system setting rather than this architecture. [just-a-reference]
kb/sources/requirements-aware-systems-research-agenda.ingest.md:44:The causal center of the proposal—semantic synchronization between changing requirements and a running architecture—is named but neither specified enough to implement nor tested. The examples show why runtime trade-offs could be useful, not that the proposed representation selects safe or effective adaptations. RELAX contributes a designer-authored uncertainty vocabulary and formal semantics, but the paper says its runtime monitoring was not implemented. Evidence cited for explanation preferences comes from a different kind of context-aware system and cannot establish that explanations derived from interacting goal and architecture models improve trust or understanding. The agenda also assumes that designers can expose the relevant goals, assumptions, measurable parameters, candidate adaptations, and model relationships; it places wholly unframeable uncertainty outside scope and does not show how genuinely new requirements or defects in that decomposition would be discovered. It therefore cannot support claims of system learning, empirical theory revision, safety, or performance improvement.
kb/sources/agent-memory-endogenous-authorization-laundering.ingest.md:33:It also gives [memory lifecycle operations](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/retire-redact-supersede-relax.md) a behavioral evaluation: retaining revoked or inactive grants can cause unauthorized action, while conservative filtering can discard valid grants. This is evidence for testing lifecycle semantics, not evidence that lifecycle fields alone suffice. Compared with [The Memory Trust Gap](./the-memory-trust-gap.ingest.md), which varies evidence already supplied to a consumer, EAL-Bench additionally measures writer formation against known authorization state and transfers frozen memories between calibrated executors. Both use oracle-correct input to isolate harmful reliance, without establishing a deployed repair process.
kb/sources/in-search-of-lost-domain-generalization.ingest.md:45:Its second role is smaller and lands elsewhere: for [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) it is a worked case of nine explicit inductive-bias bets losing to the general method under a fair protocol, without a decade of scaling hindsight — the pattern [Sutton's bitter lesson](./wikipedia-bitter-lesson.ingest.md) describes, observed in a controlled comparison instead of retrospectively.
kb/sources/in-search-of-lost-domain-generalization.ingest.md:53:3. **A protocol-parity signal that the relaxing-candidate note is missing** -- [Operational signals that a component is a relaxing candidate](../theory/operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md) lists five early signals plus composition failure as the late one. This paper demonstrates a distinct one: a specialized component's advantage disappears once the general baseline is tuned under the same declared protocol. It is cheaper to detect than composition failure and diagnoses a different fault — not that the component's theory is brittle, but that the comparison establishing its value was never fair. [deep-dive]
kb/sources/in-search-of-lost-domain-generalization.ingest.md:78:- [Codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) — is-evidence-for: nine codification bets that lost to the general method under a fair protocol
kb/sources/lessons-from-building-ai-agents-for-financial-services.ingest.md:56:2. **[bitter-lesson-boundary](../theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md)** — exemplifies the relaxing prediction. "The model will eat your scaffolding" is the bitter lesson applied to agent infrastructure. The author predicts basic skills become one-liners in two years as models improve, and describes the practical response: "write skills, delete them when unnecessary, build new ones for harder problems." This maps onto the codify-for-current-leverage-not-permanence heuristic. Critically, fiscal period normalization (10,000+ company calendars) is a clean calculator-regime counterexample — the spec IS the problem, so models will not absorb it.
kb/sources/lessons-from-building-ai-agents-for-financial-services.ingest.md:64:6. **[deploy-time-learning-the-missing-middle](../theory/retained-artifacts-enable-persistent-deployment-time-adaptation.md)** — exemplifies the full verifiability gradient. Fintool demonstrates multiple grades in production: restructured prompts (skills as markdown), eval-driven development (~2,000 test cases, PR blocked on regression), and deterministic modules (fiscal period normalization, parsing pipeline with quality scoring). The "model eats scaffolding" thesis maps onto the constrain/relax cycle.
kb/sources/building-agents-fold-subagents-into-main-loop.ingest.md:2:description: "Anthropic Applied AI advises folding routers, planners and domain subagents into one loop with skills and tool search; practitioner evidence for relaxing and context-efficiency claims"
kb/sources/building-agents-fold-subagents-into-main-loop.ingest.md:35:As evidence, it supports the context-efficiency and decomposition cluster. Its split rule depends on measured context-bloat degradation and cost or latency. That is the feasibility face and the cost face of [context efficiency is the central design concern](../theory/context-efficiency-is-the-central-design-concern-in-agent-systems.md). It also applies [feasibility is the heaviest fork's net load](../theory/feasibility-is-the-heaviest-forks-net-load.md): fold when progressive disclosure keeps the single loop under the ceiling. Its merge rule ("chain on each other's output, touch the same data, or are often called together") and its telephone-game warning are practitioner versions of two rules in [decomposition heuristics for bounded-context scheduling](../theory/decomposition-heuristics-for-bounded-context-scheduling.md): delay co-loading until interactions justify it, and do not compress away needed interfaces. The source is also a production account of relaxing under [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md). It removes classifiers, pipelines and plan rewriters, but keeps budgets, write gates, validation and approval checks in code. Moving ordering and procedure into skills while keeping hard limits in tools matches the process-versus-outcome signal in [operational signals that a component is a relaxing candidate](../theory/operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md). The flipped-task finding supports that note's preference for end-to-end tests when relaxing.
kb/sources/building-agents-fold-subagents-into-main-loop.ingest.md:43:1. **Ownership-driven decomposition as a mechanism** -- Conway's law, subagent sprawl, the Frankenprompt and localized evals suggest that some agent boundaries track team ownership, not task structure. Such boundaries resist relaxing because no single owner can measure the end-to-end effect. The proposed fix assigns ownership along a boundary that can be relaxed: a central team owns the prompt and end-to-end evals, and domain teams own skills and tools. This has reach for Commonplace's own split between instruction authors and the KB-wide gates, but rests on one source. Keep it in the log until an independent source shows the same mechanism. [experiment]
kb/sources/building-agents-fold-subagents-into-main-loop.ingest.md:45:3. **Fold-one-at-a-time evaluation method** -- Fold one component, compare with and without it, inspect which tasks flipped and not only the aggregate score, include one task per production chain and per hard rule, and repeat runs because a break appeared in one of two runs. This is a concrete relaxing test protocol that supports operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate. It can be reused when Commonplace considers dropping a forked skill or gate. [quick-win]
kb/sources/building-agents-fold-subagents-into-main-loop.ingest.md:47:5. **What stays codified after relaxing** -- Budgets, write gates, validation and approval preconditions, per-user permissions as tool-side refusals the model can read, and cheap always-relevant loading such as entity resolution stay in code. Procedure moves to skills. This is a worked example of where codification survives inside a relaxed loop. [just-a-reference]
kb/sources/duguid-on-rereading-suchman-situated-action.ingest.md:40:The Moore's Law frame **compares with** [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) and [the bitter lesson selects against unearned reach](../theory/bitter-lesson-selects-against-unearned-reach-not-against-structure.md). The shared axis is whether a limitation can be identified as compute-curable before scale tests it. The first note says it cannot. Duguid poses the same identification problem from the critic's side, but in 2012 he asserted that natural-language failures were principled, and later LLM progress partly tests that example. The Heideggerian premise he relays ("implicit assumptions cannot all be made explicit") **compares with** [Naur's human-only conclusion](../theory/naur-equates-machine-execution-with-formulated-criteria.md). Both lines of thought need an extra premise to move from inexplicit practical understanding to human-only competence. Finally, the routinization case **compares with** [Argyris on organizational learning and MIS](./argyris-organizational-learning-and-mis-1977.ingest.md), where tighter control induces ritual compliance, and with [Norman's account of silent autopilot compensation](./norman-problem-of-automation-inappropriate-feedback.ingest.md). The shared axis is hidden compensation that corrupts the evidence of how work is done.
kb/sources/goedel-machines-schmidhuber.ingest.md:83:Section 4.2 offers a **relaxed target theorem** (equation 3) with `≥` instead of `>`: the machine then rewrites itself as soon as it proves the change *will not make things worse* (printed p. 12; PDF p. 13).
kb/sources/when-code-is-free-research-is-all-that-matters-2031072399731675.ingest.md:60:4. **Taste rigidity as a failure mode.** "The researcher who was right about everything from 2018 to 2024 may be pattern-matching by 2026." This is a relaxing signal for human oracles — the same dynamic the KB describes for codified components. Could inform the relaxing-signals note or a new note on human-oracle degradation. [experiment]
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:2:description: "RELAX specifies stakeholder-bounded flexibility and monitoring assumptions for adaptive systems, without validating goals or demonstrating learned requirements revision."
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:13:domains: [requirements-engineering, environmental-uncertainty, self-adaptive-systems, fuzzy-temporal-logic]
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:17:# Ingest: RELAX — uncertainty in requirements for self-adaptive systems
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:27:RELAX extends structured natural-language requirements with operators expressing permitted temporal, quantitative, and alternative behavior under uncertainty. Requirements engineers distinguish invariants from requirements that stakeholders permit the system to relax, then specify relevant environmental properties (ENV), observable monitors (MON), their relationship (REL), and requirement dependencies (DEP). Fuzzy branching temporal logic gives semantics to expressions such as “as early as possible” without enumerating every permitted adaptation. Applying the process to an assisted-living concept document illustrates how incomplete sensing can force weaker requirements and propagate effects to dependent goals. The contribution is a language and analysis process for bounding adaptation, not an implemented controller, evidence of better health outcomes, or a mechanism for autonomously revising the authority that sets those bounds.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:39:RELAX is a concrete comparison case for separating operationalization from justification. As in [Exact implementation does not validate a requirement against its objective](../theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md), giving a requirement precise semantics does not validate its contribution to the larger purpose. The assisted-living example makes this distinction consequential: specifying eventual minimum liquid intake does not establish that the permitted delay protects health.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:41:It also clarifies the authority boundary in [Revising an improvement objective is licensed from outside it or is not improvement](../theory/revising-an-improvement-objective-is-licensed-from-outside-it.md). Stakeholders, aided by requirements engineers, decide the invariant/relaxable boundary; runtime trade-offs are licensed within that boundary. This is not a demonstration that a system can ratify a replacement terminal purpose. RELAX's “relaxation” means permitted variation in requirement satisfaction, not replacement of a component or removal of its specification.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:45:The source's adaptation mechanism is declarative permission: runtime machinery may choose behavior within specified flexibilities rather than select only from enumerated alternatives. RELAX itself does not supply that machinery. ENV/MON/REL separate what matters in the world from what can be observed and inferred; DEP records consequences for other requirements. These are useful stated objects for inspecting adaptation, but their existence does not establish learning.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:47:Against the [theory-builder definition](../theory/definitions/theory-builder.md), the evidence differs by condition. **Localized content:** the paper supplies identifiable requirements and associated uncertainty factors. **Consumption:** the intended runtime system would use their content to constrain adaptation, but the case study does not demonstrate such execution. **Content-directed criticism:** the authors' engineering analysis questions whether requirements remain satisfiable under incomplete sensing and revises their wording; it does not demonstrate an autonomous process that criticizes its own requirements or sensing assumptions. **Iteration:** the design process carries dependency consequences into further requirement changes, providing an illustrative human analysis sequence; no runtime sequence retaining criticism and using it in later rounds is evaluated. Specification artifacts retain design decisions, but persistence of runtime learning across episodes, runs, or problems is not shown.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:49:Our interpretation is therefore that RELAX supplies material an engineering process could consume and criticize, not a demonstrated autonomous theory builder. It does not measure improved capacity for future action. Nor does non-enumerative adaptation remove fixed boundaries: the requirement vocabulary, chosen invariants, and monitored properties still delimit what the proposed controller can recognize and pursue. [Learning inside a fixed decomposition inherits its mistakes](../theory/learning-inside-a-fixed-decomposition-inherits-its-mistakes.md) supplies the relevant caution: freedom within permitted satisfaction dimensions is not evidence for the adequacy of those dimensions. Whether a runtime system can discover and repair an inadequate ENV–MON relationship remains open here.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:53:1. **Separate the permitted departure from the authority permitting it.** RELAX gives a concrete requirements-engineering example of stakeholder-selected invariants and explicitly bounded flexibility. This sharpens the existing objective-revision distinction without treating behavioral adaptation as self-authorization. [quick-win]
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:54:2. **Expose the observation-to-goal inference when operationalizing knowledge work.** ENV, MON, and REL provide a compact inspection pattern: name the property of interest, the observable signal, and the inference connecting them. In an agent-operated KB, a validator result would be an observation, not automatically the quality property it is used to assess. That transfer is a proposed use of the source's distinction, not a tested KB result. [experiment]
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:55:3. **Record dependency consequences of weakened requirements.** DEP makes a relaxation's effects on other requirements explicit and prompts regression assessment. The assisted-living example illustrates why a locally acceptable weakening can impair another goal; it does not quantify the completeness of the resulting dependency analysis. [quick-win]
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:56:4. **Keep adaptation distinct from revision of knowledge.** A declarative envelope can permit unforeseen implementations while leaving the requirements and monitoring assumptions untouched. This is a useful counterexample to inferring learned methodological revision from runtime flexibility alone. [just-a-reference]
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:60:The assisted-living case demonstrates expressibility and the authors' analysis, not comparative effectiveness. Stakeholder decisions were reverse-engineered from the concept document to simulate the authority decision. There is no controlled comparison with ordinary SHALL statements or rival uncertainty specifications, no measured analyst benefit, and no deployed controller demonstrating safe adaptation. The claims about revealing dependencies and monitoring deficiencies are plausible observations from specification work, not isolated causal effects of RELAX.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:64:The ENV/MON distinction diagnoses potentially insufficient sensing but does not guarantee a correct inference from observations to environmental state. The paper assumes known physical sensors at the software-requirements stage, although its case study also motivates additional sensing technologies. It neither implements automatic discovery of missing observations nor tests revision of the requirements representation. Transfer to agent-operated knowledge work remains an analogy requiring a local test, not evidence that physical sensing and knowledge-quality assessment have interchangeable failure modes.
kb/sources/relax-uncertainty-self-adaptive-systems.ingest.md:68:Add RELAX as a bounded comparison case to [Exact implementation does not validate a requirement against its objective](../theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md), using eventual liquid intake to distinguish formalized satisfaction from a separately warranted claim about health protection.
kb/sources/dagster-asset-versioning-and-caching.ingest.md:66:fingerprinting gives it early cutoff. The source partly relaxes two limits
kb/sources/scaling-multi-agent-intelligence-substrate-centric-coordination.ingest.md:23:ScaleMAS moves coordination into a task-local, append-only datastore of linked messages. Identically prompted asynchronous agents publish completed work, search by content, and visit messages by address rather than assigning work to peers. Search and visits return at most eight messages per call; ranking adds a decaying citation weight to normalized BM25 relevance. Across four tasks and two model backbones, the paper reports better performance at matched input-plus-output token counts than independent agents, debate, a coordinator, and a shared-context baseline. Scaling extends to 128 agents on two tasks, but theorem proving plateaus while contradiction-audit recall continues improving. Within this fixed message schema, read interface, and agent harness, removing citation weight lowers eight-agent BrowseComp-Plus accuracy from 60.0% to 40.8%; this isolates ranking's contribution, not the superiority of the entire decomposition. Third-party task scores use Pass@N rather than selection of one committed answer, and contradiction-audit scoring measures relaxed recall without penalizing extra reports. The datastore is discarded after each task.
kb/sources/04-deep-learning-accelerates.ingest.md:30:Deep Speech 2 is a second strong case for [learning inside a fixed decomposition](../theory/learning-inside-a-fixed-decomposition-inherits-its-mistakes.md): it relaxes fixed linguistic intermediates into learned representations but leaves other architecture and evaluation choices fixed. The bounded WER comparison supports [exact implementation does not validate a requirement](../theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md), while the retained “kitchen-sink” engineering is compatible with [the case-level conjecture that unsupported proxy scope may explain a structured method's loss under scaling](../theory/bitter-lesson-selects-against-unearned-reach-not-against-structure.md), which diagnoses particular losses rather than guaranteeing that retained structure survives. The pedagogical essays compare with [curation as orientation](../theory/index-completeness-does-not-determine-editorial-orientation.md) because explanation changes navigability and experimentation without adding a new theorem.
kb/sources/smolensky-proper-treatment-connectionism.ingest.md:24:Smolensky proposes that intuitive cognition is best described by numerical interactions below the level of consciously available concepts. Concepts correspond to distributed activity patterns, while weights encode interacting constraints. A complete account at this lower level need not yield an exact account in conceptual rules, even though the network can be simulated on a conventional computer. The paper distinguishes two ways rules enter this picture: a proposed network can retrieve and interpret memorized instructions, or its direct performance can admit a higher-level description in rules it never retrieves. It proposes that experience generated by instruction following can train faster direct performance. A circuit model with built-in expertise illustrates rule-described competence under well-posed inputs and unlimited relaxation time; a room-feature network illustrates schema-like inference without stored room schemata. These examples motivate a relationship between precise lower-level mechanisms and useful higher-level descriptions, rather than establishing that the proposed architecture explains human cognition. The conclusion preserves the role of publicly stated scientific theories even if individual knowledge is encoded in weights.
kb/sources/smolensky-proper-treatment-connectionism.ingest.md:65:The paper is primarily a formulation of hypotheses. The proposed general linguistic interpreter, instruction-generated training, and integrated proof generator/checker are not demonstrated systems in this article. The circuit example fixes its features, legal feature combinations, and built-in expertise; its guarantee assumes well-posed problems and unlimited relaxation time. The room example fixes 40 descriptive features and derives connections from subjects' room descriptions. These examples illustrate mechanisms within chosen representations; they do not compare alternative decompositions or establish a general advantage over symbolic models. The neural correspondence is explicitly unresolved.
kb/sources/harness-as-a-language-jaz.ingest.md:77:The prompt-only designation still includes substantial supplied method guidance, environment tools, monitoring hooks, and completion guards. StuLife uses adapted tools and an explicit continuation template triggered at 70% context use. AppWorld fixes a two-level call structure and supplies full test feedback. As the [fixed-decomposition note](../theory/learning-inside-a-fixed-decomposition-inherits-its-mistakes.md) cautions, improvement inside these choices does not validate alternatives that were never compared. No implementation was inspected or executed for this ingest. The source does not establish cross-restart memory reliability, production-scale retention costs, or improvements without benchmark feedback.
kb/sources/what-is-an-agent-harness-2046980769747533830.ingest.md:47:4. **Harness-vs-framework as the bottom-up vs. top-down inversion.** The polemical move ("frameworks are configured by humans; harnesses ship as working agents") is the same inversion the bitter-lesson notes ([codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md)) describe at the model-substrate level, now restated at the runtime-architecture level. Frameworks let the human do the configuration work that ought to be deferred to the model and the convergent architecture. Connects to the [Mismanaged Geniuses ingest](./the-mismanaged-geniuses-hypothesis-2042588627260018751.ingest.md). [experiment]
kb/sources/what-is-an-agent-harness-2046980769747533830.ingest.md:69:2. **No engagement with what survives or what should be removed.** The taxonomy is entirely additive -- every section adds a component. But the [codification-and-relaxing](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) framework predicts that some current harness components will be absorbed into the model (e.g., context management, file-selection heuristics) while others will persist (e.g., permission enforcement). Dhinakaran's "push decisions to the model" gestures at this but does not identify *which* components are candidates for absorption. Same gap noted in the Vtrivedy10 ingest.
kb/sources/what-is-an-agent-harness-2046980769747533830.ingest.md:81:Write a note titled "Permission and safety form a non-pushable layer beneath the agent loop" connecting to [methodology-enforcement-is-constraining](../theory/methodology-enforcement-is-constraining.md), [agent-runtimes-decompose-into-scheduler-context-engine-and-execution-substrate](../theory/agent-runtime-analysis-should-separate-scheduling-context-state.md), and [codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) -- it would argue that the permission/safety layer is the canonical example of a decision that *cannot* be pushed to the model, and that distinguishing **judgment-pushable** from **safety-codified** decisions is what the "push decisions to the model" maturation pattern actually means. Dhinakaran's nine-component spec (permission tiers, dynamic command classification, allow/deny rules, interactive approval) and Lopopolo's structural-tests-as-permissions provide two practitioner sources; the note would name the bifurcation that resolves the apparent tension between "push to model" and "enforce beneath model" as two facets of the same maturation. This addresses the gap flagged in the connect report (no dedicated permission/safety note) and turns the surprise from the Curiosity Gate into a structural claim.
kb/sources/lifefuse-mem-lifecycle-aware-state-fusion.ingest.md:31:The source supplies a neural-memory comparison for [Retire, Redact, Supersede, And Relax Memory](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/retire-redact-supersede-relax.md): lifecycle distinctions affect behavior only when writes or reads consume them. Here a temporary exception remains locally usable while earlier evidence is protected. That differs from permanent supersession and does not establish redaction, retirement, or revision operations. The retention gains apply to supervised routing plus phase-aware checkpoint readout, so they cannot directly validate lifecycle handling in a Markdown KB.
kb/sources/lifefuse-mem-lifecycle-aware-state-fusion.ingest.md:57:Update the evaluation questions in [Retire, Redact, Supersede, And Relax Memory](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/retire-redact-supersede-relax.md) with one acquisition-controlled temporary-exception test that checks local exception use, later durable-rule recovery, and overall accuracy separately.
kb/sources/on-the-impossibility-of-obfuscating-programs.ingest.md:74:gives a counterexample robust to every natural relaxation the authors try. It
kb/sources/wikipedia-bitter-lesson.ingest.md:34:The connect pass found a tight learning-theory cluster rather than an isolated source. The strongest connection is [Fixed artifacts split into exact specs and proxy theories](../theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md): this source grounds the historical pattern that the note reframes as exact-spec artifacts versus proxy theories. It also grounds [Codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md), because Sutton's scaling pressure explains why practical systems must keep moving components between codified and learned regimes. [Oracle strength spectrum](../theory/oracle-strength-spectrum.md) extends the source by turning the binary "general methods win" lesson into a gradient based on verification quality. [Operational signals that a component is a relaxing candidate](../theory/operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md) makes that strategic warning actionable; [Spec mining is codification's operational mechanism](../theory/spec-mining-as-codification.md) is a response that codifies observed regularities instead of inventing brittle decompositions upfront. [Retained system-definition artifacts enable persistent deployment-time adaptation](../theory/retained-artifacts-enable-persistent-deployment-time-adaptation.md) connects to the learning half of Sutton's pair: retained artifact evolution gives a deployed system a persistent adaptation path without weight updates. [Constraining and distillation both trade generality for reliability, speed, and cost](../theory/constraining-and-extraction-both-trade-generality-for-reliability.md) qualifies the source by explaining why narrower artifacts still survive when their reliability, speed, and cost gains dominate. Finally, [First-principles reasoning selects for explanatory reach over adaptive fit](../theory/first-principles-reasoning-selects-for-explanatory-reach-over.md) offers the best current synthesis: reach may explain why some knowledge resists bitter-lessoning while adaptive fit gets replaced by scale.
kb/sources/wikipedia-bitter-lesson.ingest.md:38:Since the original ingestion (2026-02-23), the KB has developed substantial infrastructure around the bitter lesson: fixed-artifacts-split-into-exact-specs-and-proxy-theories.md, oracle-strength-spectrum.md, operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md, and spec-mining-as-codification.md. The extractable value below focuses on what remains NEW relative to this expanded coverage.
kb/sources/no-free-lunch-theorem-no-universal-learning-algorithm.ingest.md:30:The connect report found the strongest fit in the KB's fixed-artifact and codify/relax cluster. The source is evidence for [fixed artifacts split into exact specs and proxy theories](../theory/exact-implementation-does-not-validate-a-requirement.md), because it explains why local wins imply hidden assumptions about the problem distribution. It also supports [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md): every codified strategy is an inductive-bias bet that improves reliability, speed, or cost only where the world matches its assumptions. The A-star hopper example gives [operational signals that a component is a relaxing candidate](../theory/operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md) a simple distribution-shift exhibit, and the final "assumptions match the world" framing supports [specification strategy should follow where understanding lives](../theory/specification-strategy-should-follow-where-understanding-lives.md).
kb/sources/no-free-lunch-theorem-no-universal-learning-algorithm.ingest.md:36:1. **Codification is an inductive-bias bet** -- The essay gives a compact frame for the KB's codify/relax theory: a codified heuristic wins by assuming structure, and No Free Lunch says that assumption necessarily creates counter-worlds where it loses. This is high-reach because it applies to prompts, link labels, validators, schemas, and learned model architectures alike. [quick-win]
kb/sources/no-free-lunch-theorem-no-universal-learning-algorithm.ingest.md:40:3. **Distribution sensitivity as the operational symptom of wrong bias** -- The A-star hopper story is a clear pedagogical case for the relaxing-signals note: a heuristic can be locally correct and confidently harmful when the world violates its assumption. It is not new evidence, but it is a useful explanatory example. [just-a-reference]
kb/sources/no-free-lunch-theorem-no-universal-learning-algorithm.ingest.md:58:Update [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md): add a short paragraph in "Every codification is a bet" using No Free Lunch to state the general form of the bet. A codified artifact is an inductive bias over problem distributions; it earns reliability/speed/cost gains where its assumptions match the world and becomes a relaxing candidate where they do not. Cite this source as the accessible explainer, while preserving Wolpert/Macready or Ho/Pepyne as the formal theorem lineage if a formal citation is needed.
kb/sources/prompt-stability-code-llms-emotion-personality-variations.ingest.md:60:- [operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate](../theory/operational-signals-that-a-component-is-a-relaxing-candidate.md) — **refines**: PromptSE's emotion/personality templates provide a structured test of prompt brittleness across three template-specified rewriting levels and 14,760 variants. Non-monotonic stability across the evaluated models does not distinguish a badly-fitting theory from limited capacity, training, distillation, or architecture effects. **The note now cites this ingest for its prompt-variation method.**
kb/sources/prompt-stability-code-llms-emotion-personality-variations.ingest.md:81:2. Systematic prompt variation as dual-purpose methodology — simultaneously a verification technique (decorrelating oracle checks) and a diagnostic technique (measuring brittleness to identify relaxing candidates).
kb/sources/putting-ideas-into-words.ingest.md:30:This essay is the concise upstream anchor for the KB's human-side writing-as-thinking cluster. Its account of exact wording exposing incompleteness bears on [the human stall that LLM generation may hide](../theory/llm-generation-relaxes-goals-where-human-writing-stalls.md), while its imagined neutral stranger is a human comparator for [the adversarial human-agent loop](../theory/adversarial-loop-can-reconstruct-the-writing-is-thinking-filter.md). Exact-word commitment also resembles [constraining](../theory/definitions/constraining.md), though Graham distinguishes that commitment from the later act of testing the result. [Borretti](https://borretti.me/article/human-routers-of-machine-words) and [Grunewald](https://www.erichgrunewald.com/posts/why-i-think-you-should-almost-never-use-ai-to-write-anything-substantive/) extend the account into critiques of AI delegation; [Karlsson](https://www.henrikkarlsson.xyz/p/writing-to-think) adds conjectures, premises, and counterexamples; [Karnofsky](https://www.cold-takes.com/learning-by-writing/) adds hypothesis-guided inquiry. Those are functional comparisons, not evidence that an automated KB learns like a human: [human analogies can motivate functions without determining component boundaries](../theory/human-analogies-suggest-functions-not-component-boundaries.md).
kb/sources/on-learning-how-to-learn-learning-strategies.ingest.md:50:3. **Reversible promotion is a design primitive, not cleanup after failure** -- The stack of prior probability distributions lets the system keep a candidate modification while it appears useful and later restore old state if the evidence turns. This is a strong analogy for KB promotion: durable changes should preserve enough provenance and previous state to retire, supersede, or relax them without pretending the system never learned them. [experiment]
kb/sources/from-entropy-to-epiplexity-rethinking-information-computational.ingest.md:46:The connect report found seven direct connections. The central one is [information value is observer-relative](../theory/information-value-is-observer-relative.md): the paper gives the note a formal ML-facing measure for pattern extractability under bounded computation and explains why deterministic restructuring can create usable information for a bounded consumer even when it adds no classical information. The paper also grounds [reverse compression](../theory/reverse-compression-is-when-llm-output-expands-without-adding.md) by supplying a candidate measure for whether expanded prose adds extractable structure. It enables [minimum viable vocabulary](../theory/minimum-viable-vocabulary-is-the-naming-set-that-most-reduces.md), because prequential or requential coding could test whether a vocabulary makes more domain structure accessible. It extends [codification and relaxing navigate the bitter lesson boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) by offering a way to reason about whether an extracted regularity is genuine learnable structure or an observer-relative artifact. Finally, it grounds [context efficiency](../theory/context-efficiency-is-the-central-design-concern-in-agent-systems.md) and extends [agent context is constrained by soft degradation](../theory/soft-degradation-often-binds-before-the-hard-cap-when-evidence-fits.md) by explaining complexity-sensitive context failure as limited structure extraction, not merely token volume.
kb/sources/from-entropy-to-epiplexity-rethinking-information-computational.ingest.md:60:6. **Codification bets can be described as bets on durable structure** -- Epiplexity gives [codification and relaxing](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) a sharper distinction: codify regularities that are stable learnable structure, stay cautious around apparent patterns that only current observers can cheaply see. This is useful as a conceptual check, not yet an engineering rule. [just-a-reference]
kb/sources/the-memory-trust-gap.ingest.md:32:It also supplies a failure case for [calibrated trust in remembered knowledge](../theory/agent-memory-needs-discoverable-composable-trusted-knowledge-under.md). Models can parse dates correctly while using misleading recency to choose the wrong action. Provenance and timestamps therefore need behavioral testing with the intended consumer. Its connection to [operative supersession](../theory/agent-memory-requirements/retire-redact-supersede-relax.md) is narrower: oracle removal outperforms merely exposing conflicting items and metadata, but establishes the value of correctly resolved input, not the reliability of a supersession process.
kb/sources/norman-problem-of-automation-inappropriate-feedback.ingest.md:39:Norman's "less intelligent or more" remedy can be compared with [The augmentation-automation boundary is discrimination not accuracy](../theory/the-augmentation-automation-boundary-is-discrimination-not-accuracy.md). The shared axis is what a system must know about its own abnormal states before humans can step back. Norman's proposed signal, "compensating more than usual", is a crude self-assessment of that kind. His remark that automation "seems to function best when the workload is light and the task routine" is period illustration, not before-and-after evidence, for [Warranted transfer out of the human cut leaves people the hardest-to-warrant decisions](../theory/warranted-transfer-leaves-people-the-hardest-to-warrant-decisions.md). [LLM generation can hide a relaxed goal where human writing exposes a stall](../theory/llm-generation-relaxes-goals-where-human-writing-stalls.md) shares the axis of whether a failure announces itself where it occurs. The mechanisms differ: control saturation in Norman's cases, a plausible continuation in LLM generation.
kb/sources/why-almost-never-use-ai-to-write-anything-substantive.ingest.md:30:The chip-smuggling example compares with [A bare writing prompt does not determine its intended contribution](../theory/a-bare-writing-prompt-does-not-determine-its-intended-contribution.md): a sparse request may cue an expert to contribute distinctive judgment and find what is worth saying while cueing a model only to instantiate the requested prose form. The source is also a stress test for [An adversarial human-agent loop can reconstruct the writing-is-thinking filter](../theory/adversarial-loop-can-reconstruct-the-writing-is-thinking-filter.md): Grunewald agrees that naive delegation loses the filter but argues that post-hoc editing may still fail because generated wording anchors an expert toward passive assent and omits sensitivities the expert would have expressed while composing. His chip-smuggling audit is a concrete instance of [LLM generation relaxing a goal while hiding the dropped constraint](../theory/llm-generation-relaxes-goals-where-human-writing-stalls.md), and it illustrates the operational consequence of [Generation confidence not certifying soundness by itself](../theory/generation-confidence-does-not-by-itself-certify-soundness.md): the audit re-derives correctness instead of treating fluent generation as certification. Relative to [Borretti's earlier polemic](https://borretti.me/article/human-routers-of-machine-words), this essay independently restates the writing-as-thinking and reader-burden arguments, while adding a domain-expert error audit, clearer exceptions, and an explicit disclosure-and-trust claim.
kb/sources/why-almost-never-use-ai-to-write-anything-substantive.ingest.md:38:3. **The useful delegation boundary is whether prose is still doing epistemic search** -- The essay's exceptions separate settled rendering and coordination (copy edits, formulaic logistics, some translation) from composition that discovers the claim. This supports the scope line in the hidden-relaxation note more precisely than an artifact-level rule such as “never use AI for reports.” [quick-win]
kb/sources/hacker-news-ai-dr-ai-didnt-read.ingest.md:37:The thread is a field-report anchor for [reverse compression](../theory/reverse-compression-is-when-llm-output-expands-without-adding.md): many participants describe large textual expansions whose usable payload is small. Its strongest KB-specific role is evidence for [harmful-artifact inflow](../theory/maintenance-capacity-must-match-harmful-artifact-inflow.md), because generated comments can persist as maintenance work and as context for later agents. One domain-expert PCIe-over-TCP account concretely illustrates [hidden constraint relaxation](../theory/llm-generation-relaxes-goals-where-human-writing-stalls.md), while reported failures and counterexamples stress-test the condition in [the adversarial-loop claim](../theory/adversarial-loop-can-reconstruct-the-writing-is-thinking-filter.md): human presence is not enough unless review actively recomputes, compresses, and sometimes rejects the output. Relative to [Grunewald's substantive-writing ingest](./why-almost-never-use-ai-to-write-anything-substantive.ingest.md), this source adds heterogeneous operational reports and disagreement, but weaker attribution and no stronger empirical design.
kb/sources/dario-amodei-we-are-near-the-end-of-the-exponential.ingest.md:49:- [codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary](../theory/codification-and-relaxing-navigate-the-bitter-lesson-boundary.md) — **exemplifies**: "diffusion isn't cope" plus scaling optimism illustrates the codify/relax dynamic at the organizational level.

EXIT: 0
